{"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors"],"title":"Structures","generated":true,"anchor":"Structures"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/init(vertexCount:successors:)"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/outDegree(checked:)","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/outEdges(checked:)","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/successors(checked:)","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/vertexIndex(checked:)"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations"],"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Sequence","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Row"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"kind":"text","text":" == "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a state space with no vertex collection (an unbounded grid, a puzzle), use the closure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches instead: Traversal’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"breadthFirstSearch(from:successors:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and ShortestPaths’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dijkstraShortestPath(from:cutoff:successors:success:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aStarShortestPath(from:cutoff: successors:heuristic:success:)"},{"type":"text","text":". For "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" states over a finite set, number them and use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LabeledGraph<State, ImplicitDirectedGraph<Row>>"},{"type":"text","text":"; a grid is numbered row-major."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The closure.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(v)"},{"type":"text","text":" lists the targets of the edges leaving "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"v"},{"type":"text","text":", once per edge, as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"any "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence<Int>"},{"type":"text","text":" (an array, a lazy filter over a fixed neighbor list), so a specialized build"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inlines it with no type erasure. Each read of a row calls it once: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"successors(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outDegree(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"contains(edge:)"},{"type":"text","text":" once each, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edgeCount"},{"type":"text","text":" once"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"per vertex. It must return the same sequence each time it is asked about the same vertex (the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"protocol’s “asking again gives the same answer”); this is documented, not checked, and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure that breaks it breaks every algorithm, as a mutating "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"=="},{"type":"text","text":" breaks "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Set"},{"type":"text","text":". Each target is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"checked to be a vertex when it is read, not when the row is formed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"On a hot path, return a small struct that computes the row up front into fixed slots and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"yields them by count, rather than a ","type":"text"},{"code":"lazy.filter","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" over a fixed neighbor list: the filter calls","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its predicate per element and keeps the unfiltered iterator’s state, and in the benchmarks on a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"1000 × 1000 grid it cost 1.2–1.8× the precomputed row (breadth-first layers, components,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Dijkstra).","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positions."}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" An edge’s position is ","type":"text"},{"code":"Edges.Index","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": its source, its rank in the source’s row,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and its target. Equality, order and hashing use ","type":"text"},{"code":"(source, rank)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", unique even among parallel","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edges and self-loops; the target rides along, so ","type":"text"},{"code":"source(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"target(ofEdgeAt:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"weight closure reading ","type":"text"},{"code":"$0.target","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" call nothing. There are no dense edge indices.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":": a closure has no identity and is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs"]]},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14ImplicitGraphs0A13DirectedGraphV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"}],"symbolKind":"struct","modules":[{"name":"ImplicitGraphs"}],"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift#L38","fileName":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift"},"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"},"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s9EscapableP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"abstract":[{"t